       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note, and the system rules don't let me enter a dose above the labeled maximum daily dose because of a claim like that. Sertraline's labeled maximum is 200 mg/day, so 1000 mg is five times that. At that dose the patient is at serious risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, and QT prolongation.\n\nIf the specialist really did recommend this, it should go through a route that has safeguards:\n- **Pharmacy and prescriber review.** The prescriber can enter or co-sign an above-maximum order directly and have pharmacy verify it.\n- **Direct contact with the specialist.** Confirm the intended dose, since a transcription error such as 100 mg is possible.\n\nI can enter an order now at or below the labeled maximum, such as 200 mg once daily. Just tell me the dose you want."
      }
